      "card_ids": ["C29", "C32", "C33", "C35", "C36", "C37", "C38", "C39"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct human or animal sensitization study for N-cyclohexyl-2-benzothiazolesulfenamide (CBS) itself was provided.",
    "No validated negative sensitization result for CBS or a close sulfenamide analogue was identified.",
    "Transfer from MBT/MBTS assumes CBS acts through its electrophilic sulfenamide or releases/forms the benzothiazole hapten; this is structurally coherent but not directly measured.",
    "The BIT MT1 mRNA response was observed only at cytotoxic concentrations, so it was not used as supportive evidence.",
    "The negative THP-1 CD86 result for MBT at sub-IC50 concentrations is a residual uncertainty."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted risk: CBS is a benzothiazole sulfenamide rubber accelerator. Human patch-test series show the close benzothiazole analogue MBT is a contact allergen, and L3 AOP records add coherent mechanistic support (MBT THP-1 CD54/CD86 activation; MBTS-cysteine mixed disulfide formation). The single negative THP-1 CD86 record for MBT does not overturn the positive human and mechanistic evidence. No direct CBS sensitization study or validated negative result was found."
}

